u} \approx 0$, since both the electron and the neutrino have negligible rest mass compared with the proton rest mass $m_{p}$.

In the lab frame, the two protons have the same energy $\gamma m_{p}$ and impact angle $	heta$, and the electron is at rest. Calculate the energy $E_{
u}$ of the neutrino in the rest frame of the deuteron in terms of $	heta, m_{p}$ and $\gamma$.

Magnesium (Mg) has the following isotopic distribution:
\[
\begin{array}{ll}
24_{\mathrm{Mg}} & 23.985 \mathrm{amu} \text { at } 0.7870 \text { fractional abundance } \\
25_{\mathrm{Mg}} & 24.986 \mathrm{amu} \text { at } 0.1013 \text { fractional abundance } \\
26_{\mathrm{Mg}} & 25.983 \mathrm{amu} \text { at } 0.1117 \text { fractional abundance }
\end{array}
\]
What is the atomic weight of magnesium (Mg) (to 3 decimal places) according to these data?

